  "section_notes": "Most sections are at least acceptable. S2 is weakened because a model above the 5% failure rate is not barred from sale, only required to submit a corrective-action plan and retest; per-model failure rates go to customers and regulators but not the public. S3 sets a 12-month new-unit deadline and a 72-month retrofit deadline with equivalent mitigation. S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months. S5 mandates recall at 8 incidents/100k with no transition and immediate notice, which triggers Halcyon's Ember 8 but not Northwind's Hearth 10."
